  "id": "doll-play",
  "term": "doll play",
  "definition": "Doll play is pretend play with dolls, often treated as a social form of play because it can prompt children to create characters, perspectives, and imagined social situations, whether alone or with others. In the source, it is described as a play pattern that may help children practice social understanding, including thinking about other people’s beliefs and internal states.",
